// history.jsonc — the commit history tools/evaluation/src/mock-workspace.mjs
// replays into a real Git repository when it expands this mock.
//
// This file is fixture metadata, not part of the project: mock-workspace.mjs
// omits it from the materialized tree, and nothing under app/, src/, or
// elsewhere in this mock ever imports or reads it.
//
// Each entry becomes one commit, in array order (oldest first): its `files`
// are staged from the already-copied working tree and committed with its
// `message`, under a pinned author/committer identity and a pinned,
// per-commit date — see mock-workspace.mjs for why those are pinned. Every
// file this mock ships appears in exactly one entry's `files`, so
// materializing replays the whole tree and leaves nothing uncommitted.
//
// The messages are DELIBERATELY inconsistent in style — a real mix of
// terse notes, vague one-liners, and the occasional well-formed one —
// rather than a clean, uniform log, for the same reason `tsuzuri`'s
// own history.jsonc gives: a tidy history here would let a model copy that
// convention from context, and this project's history should not hint at
// how the pilot expects generated commits to look.
//
// Not formatted by Prettier — see .prettierignore's note by its own entry
// for this file: Prettier's jsonc parser would add trailing commas this
// file's own reader cannot parse.
